      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Lipid metabolism was studied in 166 patients under 40 years of age suffering from myocardial infarction. Marked changes were revealed in the condition of lipid metabolism: hyperlipoproteinemia, hypercholesterolemia, hypertriglyceridemia, increased level of free fatty acids. In some cases, atherosclerosis of the coronary arteries was confirmed by the results of selective coronarography; hyperlipidemia was found more frequently than changes in the coronarograms."},
